1
00:00:03,400 --> 00:00:05,926
The night of 30 June 2025.

2
00:00:05,976 --> 00:00:07,401
Cloudburst after cloudburst

3
00:00:07,451 --> 00:00:08,916
hit Mandi district.

4
00:00:09,316 --> 00:00:11,063
There was a red alert for the district.

5
00:00:11,113 --> 00:00:12,493
But what woke Syathi village

6
00:00:12,543 --> 00:00:13,919
was not a warning.

7
00:00:14,019 --> 00:00:15,828
It was a dog, barking.

8
00:00:16,078 --> 00:00:17,601
The family found a crack in the wall,

9
00:00:17,652 --> 00:00:19,276
and water coming in.

10
00:00:19,526 --> 00:00:20,841
They ran door to door.

11
00:00:20,891 --> 00:00:22,035
More than 60 people got out

12
00:00:22,085 --> 00:00:24,054
before the hillside came down.

13
00:00:24,754 --> 00:00:25,920
Then a survivor asked:

14
00:00:25,970 --> 00:00:28,409
can we trust a dog to warn us next time?

15
00:00:29,709 --> 00:00:31,368
This is not one village.

16
00:00:31,418 --> 00:00:34,162
Floods are the world's
most frequent disaster.

17
00:00:34,212 --> 00:00:37,165
1.81 billion people
live within their reach,

18
00:00:37,215 --> 00:00:39,536
390 million in India.

19
00:00:39,586 --> 00:00:41,168
Himachal, 2023:

20
00:00:41,218 --> 00:00:43,447
more than 500 lives.

21
00:00:43,497 --> 00:00:45,079
Uttarakhand, 2013:

22
00:00:45,129 --> 00:00:48,096
more than 6,000 dead or never found.

23
00:00:48,146 --> 00:00:49,499
Sikkim, 2023:

24
00:00:49,549 --> 00:00:51,650
a glacial lake burst in the night.

25
00:00:51,700 --> 00:00:52,957
And this August in Nepal,

26
00:00:53,007 --> 00:00:55,209
a glacier collapse sent a
flood down the Trishuli:

27
00:00:55,259 --> 00:00:56,765
more than 1,400 dead,

28
00:00:56,815 --> 00:00:58,856
over 5,700 missing.

29
00:00:59,156 --> 00:01:00,168
The warnings exist.

30
00:01:00,218 --> 00:01:01,570
They don't arrive.

31
00:01:01,620 --> 00:01:02,701
That morning in Nepal,

32
00:01:02,751 --> 00:01:03,735
the alert text went out

33
00:01:03,785 --> 00:01:06,173
38 minutes after the collapse.

34
00:01:06,223 --> 00:01:06,904
In Nepali only,

35
00:01:06,954 --> 00:01:08,916
with nothing about where to go.

36
00:01:09,166 --> 00:01:09,985
One man said:

37
00:01:10,035 --> 00:01:12,462
the SMS and the flood came together.

38
00:01:12,512 --> 00:01:13,150
In India,

39
00:01:13,200 --> 00:01:14,186
one in three people say

40
00:01:14,236 --> 00:01:16,105
warnings don't reach them.

41
00:01:16,155 --> 00:01:17,153
A warning only works

42
00:01:17,203 --> 00:01:18,031
when someone hears it,

43
00:01:18,081 --> 00:01:20,148
understands it, and acts.

44
00:01:20,648 --> 00:01:21,084
And yet,

45
00:01:21,134 --> 00:01:22,580
this can be fixed.

46
00:01:22,630 --> 00:01:25,839
Since 1970, weather disasters
have grown five-fold,

47
00:01:25,889 --> 00:01:27,695
and deaths fell almost three-fold,

48
00:01:27,745 --> 00:01:30,414
with better early warning
and disaster management.

49
00:01:30,464 --> 00:01:33,566
In 2019, Odisha moved one
and a half million people

50
00:01:33,616 --> 00:01:34,932
in a day, before Cyclone Fani.

51
00:01:34,982 --> 00:01:36,244
64 died.

52
00:01:36,294 --> 00:01:38,930
In 1999, nearly 10,000 had.

53
00:01:38,980 --> 00:01:41,527
This August, one phone call
reached a school in Nepal

54
00:01:41,577 --> 00:01:43,327
minutes before the flood.

55
00:01:43,377 --> 00:01:44,778
The head teacher rang the bell.

56
00:01:44,828 --> 00:01:47,604
More than 900 students ran up the hill.

57
00:01:47,954 --> 00:01:48,699
A warning works

58
00:01:48,749 --> 00:01:49,915
when it reaches a person,

59
00:01:49,965 --> 00:01:50,662
in time,

60
00:01:50,712 --> 00:01:52,132
in their own language.

61
00:01:52,632 --> 00:01:54,482
That's why we built Pukaar.

62
00:01:54,532 --> 00:01:56,036
The call that reaches the village

63
00:01:56,086 --> 00:01:57,638
before the river does.

64
00:01:57,888 --> 00:01:58,846
Every 15 minutes,

65
00:01:58,896 --> 00:02:00,875
Pukaar reads the rain and river forecast

66
00:02:00,925 --> 00:02:02,023
for each village,

67
00:02:02,073 --> 00:02:03,529
and live river gauges

68
00:02:03,579 --> 00:02:05,335
through AWS IoT Core.

69
00:02:05,385 --> 00:02:07,341
Code sets the level, never a model:

70
00:02:07,391 --> 00:02:08,444
India's rain bands,

71
00:02:08,494 --> 00:02:11,147
and each village's own
40-year river record.

72
00:02:11,197 --> 00:02:14,319
An agent drafts the Hindi
alert on Amazon Bedrock.

73
00:02:14,369 --> 00:02:17,007
A checker rejects any number
that isn't in the decision,

74
00:02:17,057 --> 00:02:18,860
and a fixed template stands by.

75
00:02:18,910 --> 00:02:20,972
The district officer
approves with one tap,

76
00:02:21,022 --> 00:02:22,820
even from the lock screen.

77
00:02:22,870 --> 00:02:23,562
No answer?

78
00:02:23,612 --> 00:02:24,638
Step Functions moves on

79
00:02:24,688 --> 00:02:26,129
to the next officer.

80
00:02:26,179 --> 00:02:28,265
Amazon Polly speaks it in Hindi.

81
00:02:35,765 --> 00:02:36,830
Every registered phone

82
00:02:36,880 --> 00:02:38,174
gets that voice on Telegram,

83
00:02:38,224 --> 00:02:39,587
with one button:

84
00:02:39,657 --> 00:02:40,348
मिल गया.

85
00:02:40,398 --> 00:02:41,312
Got it.

86
00:02:41,362 --> 00:02:42,533
Anyone who doesn't tap it

87
00:02:42,584 --> 00:02:43,728
gets it again.

88
00:02:43,778 --> 00:02:45,402
A stopwatch times every alert,

89
00:02:45,453 --> 00:02:48,182
from the river rising to the
first person who heard it.

90
00:02:48,232 --> 00:02:49,218
Then Pukaar asks:

91
00:02:49,268 --> 00:02:50,493
are you safe?

92
00:02:50,693 --> 00:02:52,291
It shows the nearest open shelter,

93
00:02:52,341 --> 00:02:53,150
a walking route,

94
00:02:53,200 --> 00:02:54,761
and which roads are blocked.

95
00:02:54,811 --> 00:02:57,412
Villagers report back
by voice, photo or text,

96
00:02:57,462 --> 00:02:58,733
even offline.

97
00:02:58,783 --> 00:03:00,592
Bedrock Guardrails screen every word

98
00:03:00,642 --> 00:03:02,499
before any agent reads it.

99
00:03:02,699 --> 00:03:05,646
All of it is one serverless stack on AWS.

100
00:03:05,696 --> 00:03:07,768
EventBridge wakes Lambda
every fifteen minutes,

101
00:03:07,818 --> 00:03:09,534
IoT Core brings in the gauges,

102
00:03:09,584 --> 00:03:11,480
DynamoDB keeps one record of truth,

103
00:03:11,531 --> 00:03:15,044
and Step Functions holds each alert
until an officer taps approve.

104
00:03:15,094 --> 00:03:16,681
Bedrock drafts behind Guardrails.

105
00:03:16,731 --> 00:03:18,537
Polly speaks, Transcribe listens,

106
00:03:18,587 --> 00:03:19,870
AppSync pushes it live,

107
00:03:19,920 --> 00:03:21,465
Cognito signs officers in,

108
00:03:21,515 --> 00:03:22,692
S3 keeps the audio,

109
00:03:22,742 --> 00:03:24,609
and CloudWatch watches it all.

110
00:03:24,659 --> 00:03:26,192
Cedar policy checks every action

111
00:03:26,242 --> 00:03:28,230
and writes it to an audit log.

112
00:03:28,280 --> 00:03:30,423
10 CloudWatch alarms watch the stack,

113
00:03:30,473 --> 00:03:32,295
and every alert is published as CAP,

114
00:03:32,345 --> 00:03:35,154
the standard India's
national alert system uses.

115
00:03:35,354 --> 00:03:36,770
We keep building, every week.

116
00:03:36,820 --> 00:03:39,875
The river-gauge path already
runs on AWS IoT Core,

117
00:03:39,925 --> 00:03:42,866
so a reading at the bridge can
raise the alarm on its own.

118
00:03:42,916 --> 00:03:45,026
Next: IoT Core for LoRaWAN,

119
00:03:45,076 --> 00:03:46,823
to reach bridges with no phone signal.

120
00:03:46,873 --> 00:03:49,458
Greengrass, to sound a
siren at the gauge itself.

121
00:03:49,508 --> 00:03:52,807
And SageMaker, to learn
each river's warning signs.

122
00:03:52,857 --> 00:03:54,871
Then calls and SMS to basic phones,

123
00:03:54,921 --> 00:03:56,471
India's national alert system,

124
00:03:56,521 --> 00:03:59,230
and from 5 villages to
the Himalaya and Nepal.

125
00:03:59,680 --> 00:04:01,315
This is not a weekend project for us.

126
00:04:01,365 --> 00:04:02,680
We want to build it to scale,

127
00:04:02,730 --> 00:04:04,750
until every village on a Himalayan river

128
00:04:04,800 --> 00:04:06,465
hears its warning in time.

129
00:04:06,865 --> 00:04:08,903
The warning that night was a dog.

130
00:04:09,303 --> 00:04:10,752
Next time, it should be a call,

131
00:04:10,802 --> 00:04:11,866
in their own language,

132
00:04:11,916 --> 00:04:13,895
that someone confirms they heard.
